{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "mephisto",
  "name": "Mephisto",
  "role": "Ranged Assassin",
  "overview": "Mephisto is a ranged Assassin who excels at following up allies' ability-chains. In other words, he works well in team compositions that are designed for \"wombo combo\". Mephisto can be devastating to the enemy team when his attacks are carefully planned. However, poor positioning and hasty use of Shade of Mephisto are easily punished by enemy Heroes who have had enough of the Lord of Hatred.",
  "strengths": [
    "Lord Of Hatred allows for liberal use of Basic Abilities",
    "Decent waveclear from Basic Abilities",
    "Has great follow-up",
    "Can secure takedowns on enemy Heroes globally with Consume Souls",
    "Can secure takedowns on fleeing enemies with Shade of Mephisto"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Somewhat reliant on allies for set-up",
    "Shade of Mephisto is easy to punish if enemies can see initial cast location",
    "Poor ability to solo-capture Mercenary Camps",
    "Susceptible to burst damage",
    "Susceptible to ganks when solo-laning"
  ],
  "synergies": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "deckard",
        "name": "Deckard Cain"
      },
      {
        "id": "e-t-c",
        "name": "E.T.C."
      },
      {
        "id": "zarya",
        "name": "Zarya"
      },
      {
        "id": "diablo",
        "name": "Diablo"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Both of Mephisto's Heroics are excellent follow-ups, and can be devastating to enemies caught by setup Heroics like E.T.C.'s Mosh Pit, Zarya's Graviton Surge, Deckard's Stay Awhile and Listen, and Diablo's Apocalypse. Mephisto's Basic Abilities also greatly benefit from strong crowd-control."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "kaelthas",
        "name": "Kael'thas"
      },
      {
        "id": "kel-thuzad",
        "name": "Kel'Thuzad"
      },
      {
        "id": "junkrat",
        "name": "Junkrat"
      },
      {
        "id": "stitches",
        "name": "Stitches"
      },
      {
        "id": "anubarak",
        "name": "Anub'arak"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Mephisto can be countered by Heroes who can quickly close into melee range, as they will avoid taking damage from Lightning Nova. The most effective counters will be able to survive some damage from Mephisto's teammates if they attempt to help him. Other heroes such as Kael'thas or Kel'thuzad can use their abilities on the shade right before Mephisto returns. Junkrat is able to place a mine on the shade and Displace you back to where you teleported. Stitches and Anub'arak are able to either Gorge or Cocoon after you cast Shade of Mephisto, negating the return teleport."
  },
